{"id":1769483,"retrievedAt":"2026-09-13T15:10:13.176Z","response":{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/mIkgpTRj784TKRkJyggIoVxghA9.jpg","belongs_to_collection":null,"budget":0,"genres":[],"homepage":"","id":1769483,"imdb_id":null,"origin_country":["JP"],"original_language":"ja","original_title":"BiSH SPARKS “DAYDREAM NATiON” EPiSODE 2 at 真駒内セキスイハイムアイスアリーナ","overview":"BiSH SPARKS “DAYDREAM NATiON” EPiSODE 2 records the headline show the Japanese idol group BiSH played at the Makomanai Sekisui Heim Ice Arena in Sapporo, Hokkaido, on 16 October 2021 — one night of BiSH SPARKS, a run of arena concerts staged across the second half of 2021 that the group pointedly never billed as a tour. Cent Chihiro Chittiii, Aina The End, Momoko Gumi Company, Hashiyasume Atsuko, Lingling and Ayuni D appear at the back of the floor during “BiSH -Hoshi ga Matataku Yoru ni-” and run the catwalk to the main stage, then pile on “GiANT KiLLERS”, “DEADMAN” and “ZENSHiN ZENREi”. A comedy interlude built on Hokkaido’s jingisukan mutton barbecue splits the set, the early rarity “Pirapiro” resurfaces, and “beautiful-sa” closes the main show. The encore gives “I have no idea.” its live premiere, Hokkaido-born Ayuni D is in tears at the last MC, and twenty-one songs end on “ALL YOU NEED IS LOVE”.","popularity":0,"poster_path":"/3IzFfPn7zz8Z6ZFTb9K56xGurmZ.jpg","production_companies":[],"production_countries":[],"release_date":"","revenue":0,"runtime":0,"softcore":false,"spoken_languages":[],"status":"Released","tagline":"","title":"BiSH SPARKS DAYDREAM NATiON EPiSODE 2 at Makomanai Sekisui Heim Ice Arena","video":false,"vote_average":0,"vote_count":0,"alternative_titles":{"titles":[]},"credits":{"cast":[{"adult":false,"gender":1,"id":2284032,"known_for_department":"Acting","name":"Cent Chihiro Chittiii","original_name":"セントチヒロ・チッチ","popularity":0.4484,"profile_path":"/6ElXLkaBILn8cp0Bbx75lWN0xLT.jpg","cast_id":1,"character":"Self","credit_id":"6aa62f365ec3d076ef71b6f0","order":0},{"adult":false,"gende